@ 7.15 - Proto-Algonquian to Ojibwe
# citation: Whimemsz, from his own work; http://home.kpn.nl/cvkolmes/ojibwe/corrCrOj.htm;
# 			Bloomfield, Leonard (1946), “Algonquian”; and “various asides and statements in dozens
# 			of different journal articles and conference papers dealing with Ojibwe or PA”
	# NB: For this sound-change set, H is “either an */h/ or */ʔ/, but we don’t know
	# 			which”.
	we e > o i
	w > ∅ / {t,r}_i
	{θ,s,h,ʔ} > ∅ / _{p,t,tʃ,k}
	θ > r
	{ʔ,h}{s,r} > s
	{ʔ,h} > ∅ / _ʃ
	{n,r} > ∅ / _r
	H > ∅ / _m
	r > s / _k
	{j,w}V:[- long] > ∅ / C_# in disyllables with V:[+ long] or in tri(-plus-)syllables
	{w,j}V:[- long] > ∅ / V:[+ long]_# (Whimemsz is unsure if this change is across-the-board or not)
	V:[- long] > ∅ / V:[- long]{w,j}_# (Whimemsz is unsure if this change is across-the-board or not)
	je:[+ long] > i:[+ long] / C_
	ja > i:[+ long] / C_C
	j > ∅ / C_
	r > n